        "tree_id": "57e2d5ae0a8de478df087da3e98fc33b729056ea",
        "message": "feat(NET-004): client prediction, reconciliation and interpolation\n\nA bounded HashTimeline in core is the client mirror of the server HashRing:\nit remembers the hash predicted at each tick so a snapshot can be compared at\nthe tick it names, never at 'now'. An unrecorded tick is unknown, never ok.\n\nPredictor applies local intents with the same stepWorld as the server (D86).\nOn a snapshot it compares, adopts the authoritative state exactly, drops intents\nwith seq <= the entity's appliedSeq, then replays survivors in (tick, seq) order.\nA mismatch is a desync: rejected, pending cleared, resync requested, never a\nsilent reconciliation (I1, GDD-NETCODE 4.3). A missing own entity is a desync too.\n\nInterpolation is presentation-only integer maths; SnapshotBuffer ignores older\nsnapshots and clears on resync. No jitter buffer, resync frame or bandwidth\nnumber is claimed here: NET-006 owns them.\n\nGDD-NETCODE 0.4 -> 0.5 (I9), including its corrupted open-questions table.\nNET-004's acc repaired to the test file; 8 broken accs remain. The D146 generator\nwas re-run against the new metrics (71 commands, 9 evidence dirs).\n\nAcceptance: net 15/15, full 105/105, verify 17/17, typecheck 0, core-math 0,\ntracer green. No dependency added; no accelerator needed.\n\nAgent: netcode-engineer\nTask: NET-004",
        "timestamp": "2026-11-18T09:07:37Z",
